# The table of `unicode/segment`, in Unicode 17.0.0: for every code point,
# the classes UAX #29 and UAX #14 cut a text by, its East Asian width, and
# the few other properties the rules and the width of a text read.
#
# Generated, never edited by hand: the Heroes program
# `generators/unicode_segment/` read the Unicode Character Database 17.0.0,
# each file held to its SHA-256, packed every code point's values into
# runs, and wrote this module whole; its `check` command says whether this
# module is still what it writes. What it read:
#
# - `LineBreak.txt`, SHA-256 e6a18fa91f8f6a6f8e534b1d3f128c21ada45bfe152eb6b1bcc5e15fd8ac92e6
# - `WordBreakProperty.txt`, SHA-256 72274cac1e6b919507db35655c3e175aa27274668a1ece95c28d2069f2ad9852
# - `SentenceBreakProperty.txt`, SHA-256 871c0c985ad95125e25b302414065a10839d068970bceb383ecec138f22a0a18
# - `GraphemeBreakProperty.txt`, SHA-256 d6b51d1d2ae5c33b451b7ed994b48f1f4dc62b2272a5831e7fd418514a6bae89
# - `EastAsianWidth.txt`, SHA-256 ea7ce50f3444a050333448dffef1cadd9325af55cbb764b4a2280faf52170a33
# - `DerivedCoreProperties.txt`, SHA-256 24c7fed1195c482faaefd5c1e7eb821c5ee1fb6de07ecdbaa64b56a99da22c08
# - `emoji-data.txt`, SHA-256 2cb2bb9455cda83e8481541ecf5b6dfda66a3bb89efa3fa7c5297eccf607b72b
# - `UnicodeData.txt`, SHA-256 2e1efc1dcb59c575eedf5ccae60f95229f706ee6d031835247d843c11d96470c

